{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat","id":1386387,"title":"What do Fair Folk eat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T06:55:41-07:00","id":1386387,"title":"What do Fair Folk eat?","content":"Hoping someone else has spotted the answer to this question and I've just missed it. Maybe in Lunars? I haven't read the whole thing yet.<br /> <br /> Fair Folk must &quot;feed on human souls&quot; in Creation or calcify (per the Cataphract and Lorelei entries in the Core). So far, so Fair Folk; this has been a key trait for a long time. But in previous editions, mechanically this was attached to Virtues; depending on their type (or specific combination of Charms) a given Fair Folk might drain your Valor, Compassion, etc. Their &quot;virtue-feeding mouths&quot;, called Graces, also happened to be the root of their magic (like Solars use Abilities or Lunars use Attributes).<br /> <br /> So in 3e, what do they eat?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:03:24-07:00","id":1386389,"title":"","content":"Don't think there is a published answer yet. Most likely answer for now is &quot;whatever you want&quot; I think ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T07:08:15-07:00","id":1386390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat#post1386387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in 3e, what do they eat?</div> </div> </div> </div>On your way to reaching them as antagonists in your game, their will be a gradually increasing field of people that were tormented or kissed or some other appropriate image, leaving them in various states of emotional and mental drain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:01:09-07:00","id":1386405,"title":"","content":"Well I guess the gameplay term would be that they eat intimacies. For instance, Adeimantus' stronger Charms can wither away intimacies that oppose him and can use his enemies' intimacies to strengthen his phantasmagoric city in the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-07-2020, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:01:25-07:00","id":1386406,"title":"","content":"Willpower, and then if they drain someone completely of will it inflicts something terrible on them. Then they get a new terrible thing each subsequent time they are WP drained to zero. And that isn't a 'canon' answer, just my suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T08:40:41-07:00","id":1386415,"title":"","content":"In my South game, the Lunars encountered a pack of Fair Folk who took the shapes of lions by day, so they could listen in on mortals and learn their names. Then by night they would stand at the edges of a settlement and call those names, luring them out to be hunted. The mortals would be subjected to hours or even days of experiencing exquisite terror at the claws of the Lion Folk. That moment when the claws sank in, <i>creating</i> that terror and trauma, destroying any courage or peace of mind they might have had, <i>that</i> was what fed them.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Which is to say, in my games they feed via touch after eroding normal, sensible Intimacies and either replacing them with mad, abstruse principles, or inflicting Derangements.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-07-2020, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T09:25:00-07:00","id":1386419,"title":"","content":"strangely I think the best example we have so far of a creature that feeds on emotions is an elemental. The Heartflame from Hundred Devils Night Parade inflames others' passions and then grows in size as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:43:28-07:00","id":1386585,"title":"","content":"I've often compared the Fair Folk to narcissists, and I think that could be an effective way of often portraying what it means for them to feed on souls; an ongoing process of forming these relationships in which your life becomes increasingly suborned to theirs while the Raksha gives you nothing in return, a process conveyed through the fantastical metaphor of you eventually becoming a true emotional husk with no independent inner life, at which point they get bored and cast you aside without regard.<br /> <br /> Heh, suddenly I'm considering the idea that a lot of Fair Folk don't want to erode your other Intimacies; they want you to keep those Intimacies and still prioritise the fae over them. Your Lorelei mistress doesn't want you to leave your wife for her, she wants you to keep loving your wife enough that every time you give in to the temptations offered you you're not only betraying her, you experience the discord of loathing yourself for that betrayal and the weakness of being unable to make a clean break while still deeply enjoying the unique pleasures of the Wyld and relying on it lacking consequence or deeper commitment.<br /> <br /> The most insidious Lorelei is the one who makes sure that the wife knows of the affair, caught in a web of hating her cheating husband while desperately hoping he never actually leaves but also disgusted at how much of a coward he is for not ending their marriage and tormenting herself with the question of what is at fault with her that causes such infidelity, despising the Raksha while also envying her.<br /> <br /> Eventually there'll be nothing left of them but (metaphorical) ghosts wandering about their lives, tied with connections they can't let go of but that no longer mean anything to them. The Lorelei is immortal, she is free from any consequence to her cruelty once she outlives it. Sometimes that means her twisted games of domination and torment are as fleeting as a dream, a flash of passion quickly forgotten and requiring immediately moving on to the next fix. Sometimes she views herself as the one constant thing, the bright spot in their dull little lives who'll live forever as a monument to the glorious story that she made of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:09:21-07:00","id":1387532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat#post1386387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoping someone else has spotted the answer to this question and I've just missed it. Maybe in Lunars? I haven't read the whole thing yet.<br /> <br /> Fair Folk must &quot;feed on human souls&quot; in Creation or calcify (per the Cataphract and Lorelei entries in the Core). So far, so Fair Folk; this has been a key trait for a long time. But in previous editions, mechanically this was attached to Virtues; depending on their type (or specific combination of Charms) a given Fair Folk might drain your Valor, Compassion, etc. Their &quot;virtue-feeding mouths&quot;, called Graces, also happened to be the root of their magic (like Solars use Abilities or Lunars use Attributes).<br /> <br /> So in 3e, what do they eat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it depends on where you find them at, in the wyld probably nothing other than their glamoured food made of wyld stuff that they don't actually need to sustain themselves, in creation they would have to follow more of creation's rules and have biological imperatives they have to follow. like eating food, drinking water, using the bathroom, that kind of stuff unless they want to eat a ton of dreams to negate the filthy creation born needs imposed on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:23:46-07:00","id":1387535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat?p=1386585#post1386585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've often compared the Fair Folk to narcissists, and I think that could be an effective way of often portraying what it means for them to feed on souls; an ongoing process of forming these relationships in which your life becomes increasingly suborned to theirs while the Raksha gives you nothing in return, a process conveyed through the fantastical metaphor of you eventually becoming a true emotional husk with no independent inner life, at which point they get bored and cast you aside without regard.<br /> <br /> Heh, suddenly I'm considering the idea that a lot of Fair Folk don't want to erode your other Intimacies; they want you to keep those Intimacies and still prioritise the fae over them. Your Lorelei mistress doesn't want you to leave your wife for her, she wants you to keep loving your wife enough that every time you give in to the temptations offered you you're not only betraying her, you experience the discord of loathing yourself for that betrayal and the weakness of being unable to make a clean break while still deeply enjoying the unique pleasures of the Wyld and relying on it lacking consequence or deeper commitment.<br /> <br /> The most insidious Lorelei is the one who makes sure that the wife knows of the affair, caught in a web of hating her cheating husband while desperately hoping he never actually leaves but also disgusted at how much of a coward he is for not ending their marriage and tormenting herself with the question of what is at fault with her that causes such infidelity, despising the Raksha while also envying her.<br /> <br /> Eventually there'll be nothing left of them but (metaphorical) ghosts wandering about their lives, tied with connections they can't let go of but that no longer mean anything to them. The Lorelei is immortal, she is free from any consequence to her cruelty once she outlives it. Sometimes that means her twisted games of domination and torment are as fleeting as a dream, a flash of passion quickly forgotten and requiring immediately moving on to the next fix. Sometimes she views herself as the one constant thing, the bright spot in their dull little lives who'll live forever as a monument to the glorious story that she made of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>don't forget the layer of the wife not being strong enough to end the marriage but hoping everyday that he comes home on time and doesn't have to &quot;work late&quot; while he is seeing his mistress","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:19:35-07:00","id":1389840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat?p=1386415#post1386415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(Which is to say, in my games they feed via touch after eroding normal, sensible Intimacies and either replacing them with mad, abstruse principles, or inflicting Derangements.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. There's something to this. Derangements act like Intimacies for the purposes of social influence. I could see the Raksha needing a victim to have an Intimacy appropriate to their feeding Grace, and commonly inflicting Derangements (like Obsession for Cup, Madness for Sword, Megrims for Ring, or Paranoia for Staff) as a shortcut.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Raksha gains nourishment when the victim is placed in a position where they could spend Willpower to resist the influence of a relevant Intimacy/Derangement, but <i>doesn't</i>; they still lose the WP but it goes to the Raksha. Holding a victim at 0 WP for an extended period is what inflicts lasting harm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat?p=1386585#post1386585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've often compared the Fair Folk to narcissists, and I think that could be an effective way of often portraying what it means for them to feed on souls; an ongoing process of forming these relationships in which your life becomes increasingly suborned to theirs while the Raksha gives you nothing in return, a process conveyed through the fantastical metaphor of you eventually becoming a true emotional husk with no independent inner life, at which point they get bored and cast you aside without regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this works for Raksha who feed with their Cup Grace (like Lorelei would do), the Grace that draws power from being desired, but there are at least three other types of feeding maw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:01:01-07:00","id":1389902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat?p=1389840#post1389840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this works for Raksha who feed with their Cup Grace (like Lorelei would do), the Grace that draws power from being desired, but there are at least three other types of feeding maw.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there are numerous kinds of parasitic, narcissistic relationship.<br /> <br /> Cult leaders, for instance. Heck, the sexual component there isn't strictly in being desirable, it's in being able to get sex simply from commanding it from people that have been conditioned to utterly submit to your rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T17:52:15-07:00","id":1390425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1386387-what-do-fair-folk-eat?p=1389902#post1389902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there are numerous kinds of parasitic, narcissistic relationship.<br /> <br /> Cult leaders, for instance. Heck, the sexual component there isn't strictly in being desirable, it's in being able to get sex simply from commanding it from people that have been conditioned to utterly submit to your rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>just take a quick search on youtube about the different types of narcissist, I'm sure you could figure out a different way each one correlates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}